WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.399 --> 00:00:03.590 align:start position:0%
 
the official announcement from the  national football league came thursday  the competition committee unanimously  recommended the rule approved in march  for instant replay of pass interference  remain in effect for the 2019 season  only that tells me that they're going to  ditch this replay review of past  interference after the 100th season in  the nfl and it also tells me they got  more to do to feel good about the new  procedures for replay review of pass  interference for the nfl's 100 season  look shireen the nfl wants nothing to  undermine this season-long celebration  this past interference replay  rule has the potential to do it because  we're either going to be talking every  monday and every tuesday and every  friday after games have been played  about too many replay reviews too many  stoppages the last two minutes of the  game taking way too long or we're going  to be talking about situations where we  think there was pass interference that  wasn't called on the field and there  should have been a replay review to  overturn it the sweet spot on this one i  think is very narrow and it's going to  be so hard for 17 different replay  officials to be on the same page this is  a potential nightmare for the nfl and i  don't think they appreciate how big of a  deal this could be and my hope is  there's somebody out there who's making  about 50 million a year to run the nfl  who cares about this as much as we do  and is committed to doing something to  fix it before the season begins  yeah and i don't know really what the  fix is at this point the coaches have  gotten their way and this is how it's  going to stand as you said for this year  and then they'll review it again and  possibly do something different or ditch  it and do nothing but the reason they've  never done a rule like this for replay  expanded replays because it is so  subjective and every person has a  different definition of exactly what  interference is i we all know what  happened at the nfc into the nfc  championship game was interference we  can all agree on that one but there's  going to be so many of these plays that  we disagree on and 99 people out of 100  in a bar are not going to agree on it  but is that one replay official going to  agree that it needs to be reviewed and  17 of them are going to have probably  differing opinions on whether that  should happen or not and it's all going  to be dependent on who that replay  official is as to whether that play gets  reviewed in real time not slowed down  but in real time and so i think that's  the difficulty of this thing and they  face an impossible thing here these  replay officials and i i feel for them  because they're going to be under the  spotlight more than they've ever been in  a really really long time  and shireen that's what got me concerned  about this earlier in the week when mike  girardi of nfl media tweeted that al  riverron was explaining it in nfl media  summit that the chargers chief's late  game pass interference call against  kansas city from week 15 on that  thursday night thriller it was past  interference called against kendall  fuller when mike williams is trying to  catch the pass in the end zone riveron  said that would have been reviewed and  it would have been determined that mike  williams also committed offensive pass  interference the  end result would have been offsetting  fouls and the chargers would have had  the ball back on the 10-yard line third  and goal  um when i saw that i thought  maybe we're not going to be activating  replay review only when it's truly  obvious like it was in the ram saints  game see i think they need just that  safety net break glass and event of  emergency type of a thing i don't want  all these rulings of past interference  to be subject to replay review because  it is so subjective and it is something  that you can look at it 10 different  ways before you realize where the  problem is i only want replay review or  whatever they use sky judge whatever to  be involved when the outcome on the  field is clearly and obviously wrong  that's the standard clear and obvious  for past interference it's got to be  clear and obvious along the lines of  what we saw in the rams saints game not  that week 15 mike williams maybe looked  like he was pushing a little bit that if  if that's subject to replay review that  feeds right into the concerns that i  have and that makes me think because al  riveron's already flagged that as  something that would be changed under  this new rule that this is going to be a  mess  yeah you're exactly right it's it's  those type of plays i think that we're  concerned about and it's going to slow  the game down which is why the nfl and  the competition committee wanted to go  back to let's have the coaches throw the  challenge flags even in the final two  minutes of each half and the coaches  said absolutely not because they don't  want to have to save their challenges  save their timeouts to be assured that  they have that when they need the  opportunity to challenge a pass  interference play so the coaches again  got their way in this thing by pushing  and pushing and pushing and this is not  at all what the nfl or the competition  committee wanted in the beginning or in  the end this isn't what they wanted  but but shireen the coaches are right  why should they have to budget a red  challenge flag for the last two minutes  of the game right in the event that  there's a major blunder like we saw in  the ram saints game i mean the nfl  should come up with a solution that  addresses the problem that happened in  january and only that problem that's  what dean blandino told deadspin earlier  this week dean blandino the former vp of  officiating if you create a rule for one  play even as obvious as that play was  you can get bad rules that way and  nobody wants that everybody wants to fix  that we want to fix what happened in the  rams saints game but we don't want it to  go farther than that right now this is  going to go farther than that and it's  going to be a problem for the nfl and  i'm just hoping the people out there who  are responsible for fixing the problem  realize it and do something about it  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

